From: gt-be98-buildroot <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] MLD: an AP MLD link may be any BSS of its interface, not only bss[0]

On this AP (gt-be98) each radio has one hostapd configuration: its plain BSSes first (the radio's primary runs the
CAC and brings the radio up), the AP MLD link as a later bss=. Every MLD loop below walked the interfaces and looked
only at each interface's bss[0]. A link at bss[1..] was invisible to them:
- hostapd_notif_disassoc() / hostapd_notif_disassoc_mld(): a leaving ML station's copy on such a link was never
  freed. Its next association was refused while adding that link ("MLD: link: Station already exists", status 1)
  until the copy expired (open-wifi q471: an MLD-capable client could not rejoin after leaving);
- ap_sta_ml_disconnect(): an AP-initiated disassociation / deauthentication missed that link's copy;
- ieee802_1x_ml_set_sta_authorized(), ap_sta_set_vlan(), ap_sta_bind_vlan(): the partner links' authorized flag and
  VLAN missed it;
- switch_link_scan(), the HT-scan result for the other links, the Reconfiguration Multi-Link element.

- ieee80211_ml_process_link(): a link station a PREVIOUS association of the MLD left behind (disassociated or
  deauthenticated, waiting for its removal timer: an AP-initiated deauthentication keeps every link's station
  AP_MAX_INACTIVITY_AFTER_DEAUTH) refused the new association ("MLD: link: Station already exists"), and its later
  removal took the new association's link station out of the driver (q472: the client re-associated on two links
  and passed no data). It is now freed before the new link station is added; a still-associated one is refused as
  before.

hostapd_iface_ml_bss(iface, hapd) returns the BSS of @iface that is an ML partner of @hapd at any index, else bss[0]
(the previous behaviour), and replaces iface->bss[0] at those ten places. No behaviour changes when every MLD link
is its interface's first BSS.

Test: package/gt-be98-os/test/build-hostapd-ml-partner-test.sh (host build, --selftest with two controls).

---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -5272,6 +5272,28 @@
 }
 
 
+/* gt-be98 0007: the BSS of @iface that is affiliated with @hapd's AP MLD, at ANY BSS index. An MLD link need not be
+ * its interface's first BSS: a radio's configuration may put its plain BSSes first and the AP MLD link as a later
+ * bss= (the radio's CAC and primary then come first). The loops below looked at bss[0] only, so every station record
+ * of a link at bss[1..] was invisible to them: a leaving ML station's partner copy stayed ("MLD: link: Station already
+ * exists" on its next association). Returns bss[0] when no BSS of @iface is a partner (the previous behaviour). */
+struct hostapd_data * hostapd_iface_ml_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					   struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	size_t j;
+
+	if (hapd && hapd->conf && hapd->conf->mld_ap && iface->bss) {
+		for (j = 0; j < iface->num_bss; j++) {
+			struct hostapd_data *b = iface->bss[j];
+
+			if (b && b->conf && hostapd_is_ml_partner(hapd, b))
+				return b;
+		}
+	}
+	return iface->bss[0];
+}
+
+
